hadiths[40]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3822","The same is narrated about Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"3823","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, says: When a man closes the door and lowers the veil or looks at a woman's seventies, it becomes obligatory to pay dowry on him, and it is obligatory on the woman to perform the `iddah, and she gets a share of the inheritance."
"3824","Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever looks at a woman with her veil removed, the payment of dowry becomes obligatory on him, regardless of whether he has intercourse with her or not."
"3825","Sulaiman bin Yasar narrates: Harith bin Haqm married a woman, he closed the door, then he left the room and divorced that woman. In our view, Harith should be confirmed, asked Sayyiduna Zayd, \If this woman becomes pregnant"," will you stone her?\"" Marwan replied no"," Sayyiduna Zaid said"," In such a situation"," the woman's statement will be confirmed."""
"3826","According to Saeed bin Musayb, there is nothing wrong with a person marrying a fifth wife after divorcing his (fourth) wife, whether she (the divorced woman) is pregnant or not."
"3827","Hasan Basri, Saeed bin Musayb, and Khalas bin Amr say: (What they say is in the next hadith) These gentlemen say: When a man divorces his wife and she is pregnant, even if he wishes, he can marry her sister during the Idda period."
"3828","We are informed by Hammad, who narrates on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who narrated this (the above hadith) from his father (Urwa bin Al-Zubayr)."
"3829","Qasim bin Muhammad and Urwa bin Zubair say: A person who has four wives and divorces one of them, he can marry (the fourth) whenever he wants, he will not arrange for the period (of his former wife) to pass."
"3830","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A slave can have two marriages (simultaneously), and he can give two divorces."
"3831","Imam Jafar Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates this statement of Imam Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) with reference to his father (Sayyidna Imam Baqir (may Allah be pleased with him)) with reference to his grandfather (Imam Zain al-Abidin may Allah be pleased with him): Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said about a person who bought a slave girl, had intercourse with her, and then discovered a defect in the slave girl, he says that the slave girl will remain with that person, and her price will be reduced according to the defect. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: If the ruling is similar to that of a Hoji, then that person will return the woman, and along with it he will also pay the ``aqr (compensation paid in the case of a suspected wati), then it will be similar to the ``Ijarah''. (This is the ruling) When he has intercourse with this slave girl, she will be his and her value will be reduced according to the defect."
"3832","Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates this statement of his father (Imam Baqir, may God be pleased with him): Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, says: When a person buys a slave girl, then has intercourse with her, and after having intercourse with her, finds a fault in her, then he will take back the price (part of the price) according to the fault. This tradition is \Mrsal\""."""
"3833","Imam Jafar Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) quoted his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir may Allah have mercy on him) on the authority of Imam Zain al-Abidin (may Allah have mercy on him) as saying of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): (The buyer will not return the defective maidservant), but the decrease in price due to this defect will be returned to him. This tradition is also transmitted."
"3834","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: If she is a female slave, then the buyer will return half of the Usher (ie, twentieth part of the original price) with her, and if she is a virgin, he will return usher (ie, one-tenth of the original price). The narrator named Amir has not found the time of Sayyiduna Umar."
"3835","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When a man (buyer) has intercourse with a slave girl, then it will become a transaction, but if the buyer develops a defect in her before intercourse with the slave girl, then he has the right to keep her if he wishes, and to return her if he wishes."
"3836","Raja bin Hayyah narrates: Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about Umm-Wald's Iddah, and he said: Do not confuse the religious rules in front of us. This same tradition along with another chain of transmission has been transmitted as a chain of transmission to Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3837","Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Do not confuse the Sunnah of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in front of us. The Idah of her (son's mother) will be the same as the Idah of a widow, i.e. four months and ten days."
"3838","The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of narrators. The narrator named Qubaysa did not listen to the hadiths from Sayyiduna bin As, may Allah be pleased with him."
"3839","Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: Do not confuse the Sunnah of our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"3840","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3841","Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: When the master of Umm Ould Ka died, her Iddah will be four months and ten days, and when she is freed, her Iddah will be three menstrual periods. This hadith is muquf, and this is correct, this hadith is also transmitted, because the narrator named Qubaysa did not hear the hadiths from Sayyidna Amr bin Al-Aas."
"3842","Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: We will not play with the rules of our religion (i.e. we will not state wrong rules). A free woman is free and a slave girl is a slave girl."
"3843","Sayyidna Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, says: The period of the mother's son is the same as the period of a free woman (says a narrator named Abdullah bin Ahmad). Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The period of the mother's son is the same as the period of a free woman."
"3844","It was narrated on the authority of Qubaysa bin Dhuwayb that Sayyid Na Amr bin As said: The rite of a son is the rite of a free woman."
"3845","Abu Hasan narrates: I asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) about a slave whose wife is a maidservant and then he gives her two talaqs, then they both become free together, then Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Abbas said: Now if he wants a man, he can give her a message of marriage. The Prophet (PBUH) has given this decision."
"3846","Abu Hasan narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) about a slave whose wife is a maidservant, and then he divorces her twice, and she divorces him, and then they both become free, then whether that man can give the message of marriage to this woman."
"3847","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “When a slave girl is the wife of a man and that person gives her two divorces, then he buys her, then that slave woman will not be lawful for him until he remarries (a widow or divorcee)."
"3848","Abu Uthman narrates: A woman came to the service of Sayyiduna Umar (RA) and said: Her husband has developed insanity, so Sayyidna Umar (RA) ordered her to wait for four years, and then (after four years) Sayyidna Umar (RA) ordered the guardian of the man suffering from insanity to divorce the woman."
"3849","Narrated by Sayyidna Mughirah bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The wife of a missing person will remain his wife until the news (of the missing person's death) reaches her."
"3850","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sayyidna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyidna Abd bin Zam’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) presented a case to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the son of the maidservant of Zam’ah. To obtain the son of a slave girl because he is my (illegitimate) child, Abd bin Zamaa said, O Messenger of Allah (that boy is my brother, who is the son of my father's slave and was born in my father's bed. The Prophet saw a clear resemblance to Utbah, but the Prophet said, O Abd Zamaa, you will get this, because the offspring is counted as the owner of the bed, and O Suda). Bint Zam'ah you cover it. Imam Malik, Salih bin Qaisan, Shuaib bin Abu Hamzah, Ibn Jarij, the nephew of Muammar bin Rashid, Yunus bin Sa'd, Sufyan bin Hussain and other narrators have followed it. In the tradition of Malik, Muammar, Laith, Saleh bin Qaisan, Ibn Ishaq and other narrators, there are these words: He did not see Sayyida bint Zam'ah."
"3851","Zayd bin Aslam says about this statement of Allah Ta'ala, Zalik Idni al-Tawlawa: It is better than not having many people who are under your protection."
"3852","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed a widow that if she wanted, she could spend her `iddah outside her home. This hadith has been narrated only by Abu Malik Nakhai with authority and this narrator is weak and the narrator named Mahbub is also weak."
"3853","Saeed bin Basheer narrates: He asked Qatadah about Zahar, so Qatadah told me that Sayyidna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith to me: Sayyidna Aus bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) performed Zahar with his wife Khawaila bint Thaalba. The verse related to Zahar was revealed. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Sayyiduna Aws, he said, “I do not have the capacity for it.” Feed, they said, I do not even have this position, but if you help me and act with mercy (then I can do that)."
"3854","Sayyiduna Salama bin Sakhr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him a vessel containing fifteen Sa'a (of grain). (The narrator narrates) In this way every poor man got a mud."
"3855","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, a man appeared with his wife, then he saw the shine of her leg in the moonlit night, so (he was able to pass Qa Abuna on himself) and had intercourse with her. \Before they have intercourse with each other (expiation must be paid) (the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him) said"," \""Now do not have intercourse with your wife until you have performed expiation."""
"3856","Sayyiduna Salama bin Sakhar (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Salama Bin Sakhar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed him to go to Banuflan and collect a wasaq of dates from them and give them (one wasaq) to sixty poor people."
"3857","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, says about the person who performed Zahaar, if he had intercourse before paying Kaffaar, then it will be necessary for him to pay two Kaffaras."
"3858","Qabaisa bin Dhuwaib says: Two expiations will be required on such a person."
"3859","Sayyiduna Salama bin Sakhr (RA) narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH), he made an appearance with his wife, and then before paying Kaffara, he also had intercourse with her."
"3860","Sayyiduna Salama bin Sakhr (RA) narrates this saying of the Prophet (PBUH) regarding the person who makes Zahar, who has intercourse (with a woman) before performing the expiation, his expiation will be the same."
"3861","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I am ready to argue with anyone who wants to discuss the issue of not having sex with a slave girl."
